From: Louis Maliyam <louis@nexthop.ai>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:54:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] misc: amd-apml: sbrmi: retry the 1-byte register-size probe

On SB-RMI rev 0x10 (AMD Fire Range), the 2-byte register read the
driver tries first is answered with an abnormal condition, and the
AST2700 I2C controller then fails the next two transfers on the bus
(EAGAIN, EPROTO, ENXIO). The driver falls back to a 1-byte read exactly
once, which always lands on one of those failures, so the regmap is never
configured. Every hwmon read then repeats the whole probe and fails with
ENXIO after about 0.6 s, which makes `sensors` take about 20 s on
nexthopbmca7c.

Retry the 1-byte read like the 2-byte one, also when it reads back the
0xFF revision that the driver says a 2-byte read can leave cached on rev
0x10. It succeeds on the second or third attempt and the regmap is cached
for the rest of the boot.

Signed-off-by: Louis Maliyam <louis@nexthop.ai>
---
 drivers/misc/amd-apml/sbrmi.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/amd-apml/sbrmi.c b/drivers/misc/amd-apml/sbrmi.c
index f68cd41..c637576 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/amd-apml/sbrmi.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/amd-apml/sbrmi.c
@@ -669,7 +669,16 @@ static int sbrmi_i2c_identify_reg_addr_size(struct i2c_client *i2c, u32 *size, u
 	 */
 	if (ret != I3C_I2C_MSG_XFER_SIZE || *rev == 0xFF) {
 		reg_size = SBRMI_REG_ADDR_SIZE_DEF;
-		ret = sbrmi_i2c_reg_read(i2c, reg_size, rev);
+		/*
+		 * A 2-byte read of SB-RMI rev 0x10 leaves the I2C controller failing
+		 * the next transfers and can leave 0xFF cached, so retry this too.
+		 */
+		for (i = 0; i < MAX_RETRY; i++) {
+			ret = sbrmi_i2c_reg_read(i2c, reg_size, rev);
+			if (ret == I3C_I2C_MSG_XFER_SIZE && *rev != 0xFF)
+				break;
+			usleep_range(10000, 20000);
+		}
 		if (ret != I3C_I2C_MSG_XFER_SIZE) {
 			pr_err("I2C reg read failed with return value:%d\n", ret);
 			return ret;
